<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="generator" content="qpcr-assay-check {{ r.tool.version }}">
<title>{{ assay.assay_name }} – assay evaluation record ({{ r.overall.verdict.value }})</title>
<style>
:root {
  --ink: #17222D; --muted: #55636F; --paper: #F4F6F8; --panel: #FFFFFF; --rule: #D3DBE2;
  --pass: #1F7A5A; --pass-bg: #DDF0E7;
  --warn: #9A5F00; --warn-bg: #FBEBC8;
  --fail: #B23B3B; --fail-bg: #F6D9D9;
  --incomplete: #46566B; --incomplete-bg: #DCE2EA;
  --info: #55636F; --info-bg: #E6EAEE;
  --serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif;
  --sans: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { background: var(--paper); }
body { margin: 0; color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; }
main { max-width: 64rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
h1, h2, h3, table, .chip, .meta, .rec { font-family: var(--sans); }
h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 .35rem; }
h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 3rem 0 .75rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 .5rem; }
p { margin: .6rem 0; max-width: 46rem; }
.meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
.meta code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .8rem; word-break: break-all; }

.verdict { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 0 2rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
  background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left-width: 10px; padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem; }
.verdict.v-PASS { border-left-color: var(--pass); }
.verdict.v-WARN { border-left-color: var(--warn); }
.verdict.v-FAIL { border-left-color: var(--fail); }
.verdict.v-INCOMPLETE { border-left-color: var(--incomplete); }
.verdict .word { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 2.6rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
.v-PASS .word { color: var(--pass); } .v-WARN .word { color: var(--warn); }
.v-FAIL .word { color: var(--fail); } .v-INCOMPLETE .word { color: var(--incomplete); }
.verdict .label { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: .25rem; }
.verdict ul { margin: .3rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
.verdict li { margin: .2rem 0; }
@media (max-width: 40rem) { .verdict { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem 0; } }

.chip { display: inline-block; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; padding: .1rem .5rem; border-radius: 3px; white-space: nowrap; }
.s-PASS, .s-evaluated-PASS { background: var(--pass-bg); color: var(--pass); }
.s-WARN { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn); }
.s-FAIL { background: var(--fail-bg); color: var(--fail); }
.s-INFO, .s-none { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info); }
.s-INCOMPLETE { background: var(--incomplete-bg); color: var(--incomplete); }

table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .88rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: .45rem .65rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
thead th { background: #EAEFF3; font-weight: 600; }
tr.group th { background: #F1F4F7; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
td.num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
td.note { color: var(--muted); }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
.seq { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .92rem; letter-spacing: .04em; word-break: break-all; }
.seq .tail { font-weight: 700; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
pre { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .78rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: .75rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; line-height: 1.35; }
details { margin: .75rem 0; }
summary { cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: .9rem; }
summary:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #3B5B7A; outline-offset: 2px; }
figure { margin: 1rem 0; } figcaption { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); font-family: var(--sans); }
.notice { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: .9rem 1.1rem; }
.notice p { margin: .35rem 0; }
footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }

@media print {
  html { background: #fff; } main { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
  .verdict, table, pre, figure, .notice { break-inside: avoid; }
  h2 { break-after: avoid; } details:not([open]) > *:not(summary) { display: block; }
}
</style>
{% if plotly_js %}<script>{{ plotly_js }}</script>{% endif %}
</head>
<body>
<main>
{% macro chip(status) %}<span class="chip s-{{ status }}">{{ status }}</span>{% endmacro %}

<header>
  <h1>{{ assay.assay_name }}</h1>
  <p class="meta">
    Assay evaluation record · generated {{ r.generated_at }} · qpcr-assay-check v{{ r.tool.version }} ·
    run <code>{{ r.run_id }}</code><br>
    Inputs hash (SHA-256): <code>{{ r.inputs_hash }}</code>
  </p>
</header>

<section class="verdict v-{{ r.overall.verdict.value }}" aria-labelledby="verdict-h">
  <div>
    <div class="label" id="verdict-h">Overall verdict{% if r.mode == 'qc-only' %} (oligo QC only){% endif %}</div>
    <div class="word">{{ r.overall.verdict.value }}</div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p>{{ verdict_meaning }}</p>
    {% if r.overall.rationale %}
    <ul>
      {% for line in r.overall.rationale %}<li>{{ line }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<h2>Sections evaluated</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Result</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in r.sections %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ s.title }}</td>
    <td>{% if s.verdict %}{{ chip(s.verdict.value) }}{% else %}<span class="chip s-none">Not evaluated</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="note">{{ s.note }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2>Assay as evaluated</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Forward primer</th><td>{{ assay.forward | seq_html }} <span class="meta">{{ assay.forward | length }} nt</span></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Reverse primer</th><td>{{ assay.reverse | seq_html }} <span class="meta">{{ assay.reverse | length }} nt</span></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Probe</th><td>{{ assay.probe | seq_html }} <span class="meta">{{ assay.probe | length }} nt</span></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Reporter / quencher</th><td>{{ assay.probe_reporter or 'not specified' }} / {{ assay.probe_quencher or 'not specified' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Probe modifications</th><td>{{ assay.probe_modifications | join(', ') or 'none declared' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Template</th><td>{{ assay.template_type.value }}{% if assay.template_type.value == 'RNA' %} (reverse transcription step assumed){% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Intended target</th><td>
      {% if assay.target.taxid %}taxonomy ID {{ assay.target.taxid }}{% endif %}
      {% if assay.target.accession %}{% if assay.target.taxid %}; {% endif %}reference {{ assay.target.accession }}{% endif %}
      {% if assay.target.gene %}; gene {{ assay.target.gene }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% if assay.oligo_source %}<tr><th scope="row">Oligo source</th><td>{{ assay.oligo_source }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if assay.notes %}<tr><th scope="row">Notes</th><td>{{ assay.notes }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">The last five nucleotides of each sequence, the 3′ end, are underlined.</p>
{% set degenerate = qc.oligos | selectattr('degenerate') | list %}
{% if degenerate %}
<p>Degenerate oligos were expanded and every variant was evaluated; the worst variant decides each status:
  {% for o in degenerate %}{{ o.role }} → {{ o.n_variants }} variants{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Oligo quality control</h2>
{% if qc.tm_unreliable_reasons %}
<div class="notice"><p><strong>Tm reliability.</strong> The probe carries {{ qc.tm_unreliable_reasons | join(', ') }}.
  Nearest-neighbour Tm and dimer estimates do not model these modifications; use vendor-specific values.</p></div>
{% endif %}
{% for c in charts %}
<figure>
  {{ c.html }}
  <figcaption>{{ c.caption }}</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endfor %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Value</th><th>Result</th><th>Rule applied</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for title, items in groups %}
    <tr class="group"><th colspan="4">{{ title }}</th></tr>
    {% for c in items %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ c.name }}{% if c.message %}<br><span class="meta">{{ c.message }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ c.display }}{% if c.unit %} {{ c.unit }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ chip(c.status.value) }}</td>
      <td class="note">{{ c.rule }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if qc.amplicon_note %}<p class="meta">{{ qc.amplicon_note }}</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Hairpins and dimers</h2>
<p>Calculated at the annealing temperature of {{ r.config.reaction.annealing_temp_C }} °C
  (Na⁺ {{ r.config.reaction.na_mM }} mM, Mg²⁺ {{ r.config.reaction.mg_mM }} mM, dNTP {{ r.config.reaction.dntp_mM }} mM).
  A structure is flagged when its melting temperature reaches
  {{ r.config.thresholds.structures.warn_tm_c }} °C (WARN) or the
  {% if r.config.thresholds.structures.fail_tm_c is none %}annealing temperature{% else %}{{ r.config.thresholds.structures.fail_tm_c }} °C{% endif %} (FAIL).
  “3′ end” rows test whether the 3′ end of the first oligo can anneal to the second and be extended.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Structure</th><th>Tm (°C)</th><th>ΔG (kcal/mol)</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in qc.structures %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ s.label }}{% if s.n_total > s.n_evaluated %}<br><span class="meta">{{ s.n_evaluated }} of {{ s.n_total }} variant combinations evaluated</span>{% endif %}
      {% if s.variant %}<br><span class="meta">worst case: {{ s.variant }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ s.tm_c | tm }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ s.dg_kcal | dg }}</td>
    <td>{{ chip(s.status.value) }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% if s.ascii_lines %}<tr><td colspan="4"><pre>{{ s.ascii_lines | join('\n') }}</pre></td></tr>{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">Tm “none” means no structure was found; “&lt; 0” means the only structure is far too weak to matter.
  Thermodynamic values are estimates from primer3 nearest-neighbour parameters.</p>

{% if qc.amplicon %}
<h2>Amplicon</h2>
{% set a = qc.amplicon %}
<div class="scroll"><table><tbody>
  <tr><th scope="row">Reference amplicon</th><td>{{ a.input_length_nt }} nt</td></tr>
  {% if a.product_length_nt %}<tr><th scope="row">Primer-defined product</th><td>{{ a.product_length_nt }} bp, {{ '%.1f' % a.product_gc_percent }}% GC</td></tr>{% endif %}
  {% for site in [a.forward_site, a.reverse_site, a.probe_site] if site %}
  <tr><th scope="row">{{ site.oligo | capitalize }} site</th><td>{{ site.start }}–{{ site.end }} ({{ site.strand }}), {{ site.mismatches }} mismatch(es)</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Not yet evaluated</h2>
<div class="notice">
  <p>This version of qpcr-assay-check evaluates oligo quality only. Specificity against public sequence
    data, off-target amplicons, exclusivity, inclusivity and comparison with earlier runs arrive in later releases
    (see the sections table). <strong>No sequence has been searched against any database in this record</strong>,
    and no data was sent to NCBI{% if r.network_used %} (this run used the network){% endif %}.</p>
</div>

<h2>Methods</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table><tbody>
  <tr><th scope="row">Software</th><td>qpcr-assay-check {{ r.tool.version }}; Python {{ r.environment.python }}; primer3-py {{ r.environment['primer3-py'] }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Platform</th><td>{{ r.environment.platform }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Melting temperature</th><td>{{ r.config.reaction.tm_method }} nearest-neighbour model, {{ r.config.reaction.salt_correction }} salt correction;
    primers {{ r.config.reaction.primer_nM }} nM, probe {{ r.config.reaction.probe_nM }} nM</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Structures</th><td>primer3 thermodynamic alignment (hairpin, homodimer, heterodimer, 3′-end) at {{ r.config.reaction.annealing_temp_C }} °C</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">3′ end stability</th><td>Sum of SantaLucia (1998) nearest-neighbour ΔG°37 over the last five nucleotides (informational)</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Run mode</th><td>{{ r.mode }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Database, BLAST parameters, RIDs</th><td>Not applicable: no database search was performed</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<details>
  <summary>Effective configuration (thresholds and conditions applied)</summary>
  <pre>{{ config_yaml }}</pre>
</details>

<h2>Limitations</h2>
<p>Default thresholds are starting points drawn from common TaqMan design guidance; they are not acceptance
  criteria and must be reviewed by the laboratory. Melting temperatures and dimer energies are computational
  estimates and depend on the reaction conditions entered. Structures are searched at the annealing temperature, so a
  hairpin or dimer that forms only at lower temperatures (for example during reaction set-up) may not be reported, and
  the same oligo can be flagged at one annealing temperature and not at another. Modified probes (MGB, LNA, ZEN and
  similar) are not modelled. These results describe the oligo sequences only: nothing here says how the assay behaves
  against real specimens or real off-target sequences.</p>

<h2>Required statements</h2>
<div class="notice">
  <p><strong>In silico analysis does not replace experimental validation.</strong> The outcome of this evaluation
    must be interpreted together with wet-laboratory verification of the assay.</p>
  <p><strong>The laboratory is responsible for verifying this software within its own quality system</strong>
    before relying on its output. qpcr-assay-check is provided without warranty (Apache License 2.0).</p>
</div>

<footer class="meta">
  Record {{ r.run_id }} · generated {{ r.generated_at }} (UTC) · qpcr-assay-check v{{ r.tool.version }} ·
  inputs hash {{ r.inputs_hash[:16] }}… · schema {{ r.schema_version }}
</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
